==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Uralic|ware|lang=fi}}, a cognate of the Hungarian {{term|varjú}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈʋɑris]|lang=fi}}
* Hyphenation: va·ris

===Noun===
{{fi-noun|vari|type=seos}}

# A [[hooded crow]] or [[grey crow]], ''Corvus cornix''.
# Any [[crow]].

====Usage notes====
Until recently [[carrion crow]] (''[[nokivaris]]'', which is rarely seen in Finland) was believed to be just a black variant of [[hooded crow]] or [[grey crow]] (which is common in Finland). Therefore many dictionaries give "carrion crow" as translation for '''''varis'''''.

====Synonyms====
'''any crow'''
* [[varislintu]]

====Declension====
{{fi-decl-seos|vari}}

====Compounds====
* [[mustavaris]]
* [[nokivaris]]
* [[varislintu]]

